# Synthesized-logic review of 8-riscv-dv against main, and a Linux RTL boot (issue #8)
# 2026-10-23 UTC. Question: does the branch change the synthesized logic only where its
# three core fixes say it does, and does the simulation-only commit-trace probe disappear
# from every synthesis view?
#   A = main 9da0006 (the sigil-linux-f2-2026-10-22 release)
#   B = origin/8-riscv-dv f2393973 (rtl/ identical to 37aa1d7, the last code change, and to 65a48ae)
# The fixes: 63a50a5 viota.m vs2 is one mask register; 63a50a5 .vf scalars NaN-box checked at
# SEW=32; 3ae351d PMP decides on all bytes of an 8-byte access. Trace probe: d9067a9, b4bb704,
# 862868c, e1c4338 (`ifndef SYNTHESIS in sigil_core.sv and sigil_csr.sv).
# Define sets, the five of scripts/synth_view_diff.sh: SYNTHESIS (FPGA CL build
# synth_cl_sigil.tcl, f0 OOC, the unit flows), +SIGIL_SRAM_FAKERAM45 (ORFS nangate45),
# +SIGIL_SRAM_SKY130 (ORFS sky130hd), +SIGIL_SRAM_OREG, +SIGIL_VRF_OREG (f0 option, #53).
# Every synthesis flow in the tree passes SYNTHESIS.
# Tools: Mac (Apple M3, macOS 26.6.2): Verilator 5.044, sv2v 0.0.13, Yosys 0.69+post and its
# yosys-abc. Linux boot: sigil-verify (32 vCPU c7i.8xlarge, Ubuntu 24.04), Verilator 5.048 (deps/).
# Scripts: tools/ (tools/make_trees.sh makes the compared trees; every result below reruns from them).

== Result

Two modules differ in synthesized logic, sigil_core and sigil_csr, identically in all five
define sets. The other 41 modules (46 design units) are byte-identical after preprocessing.
Every difference is one of the three fixes:
  sigil_core  viota.m: ex_vs2_log2 (4 bits, the vs2 alignment check of the illegal-
              instruction logic)
              .vf NaN-box: the vector unit's scalar_i (64 bits)
              PMP: the two new sigil_csr inputs pmp_wide_b_i = (mem_size_code == 3) (the
              data port) and pmp_wide_c_i = 1 (the page-table walker)
  sigil_csr   PMP: pmp_allow_b_o (data) and pmp_allow_c_o (walker); nothing else, and not the
              fetch port pmp_allow_a_o
With the three fixes reverted, the branch's sigil_core is proven equivalent to main's (all
10,968 $equiv points). That covers the trace probe, the mem_size_code rewrite of the
byte-enable case select, and the vec_frs1 wire. The trace probe leaves nothing in any
synthesis view: no trace identifier remains after preprocessing or sv2v, and the flip-flop
counts match main's. The PMP difference is characterized by SAT for all register contents:
same verdict for every access except an aligned 8-byte one whose deciding entry (the lowest-
numbered entry matching either 4-byte word) matches only one word, and such an access is
denied.
Linux RTL boot on the branch: SIGIL_LINUX_BOOT_OK at 261,247,447 cycles, the same as main
(the release gates' figure, and main rerun here beside the branch). The UART logs are byte-
identical: 890 lines, sha256 a14fee2d...

